{
  "kanji": "筆",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 筆\ntitle: brush; writing\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 12\nradical: 竹\nradicalNumber: 118\nonyomi: [ヒツ]\nkunyomi: [ふで]\ndistractors: [律, 建, 雪]\n---\n\n# 筆 — brush; writing\n\n**Strokes:** 12 · **Key (radical):** 竹 (no. 118) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n筆 concerns a writing or painting brush and, by extension, writing or composing text. In compounds it can contribute a writing implement without saying that the object has traditional brush hairs.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Picture the bamboo-shaped top as the handle above the 聿-shaped writing part. This is a modern-shape memory aid, not a verified account of an ancient hand or brush.\n\nThe canonical key is [竹](竹.md), no. 118, visible as ⺮ at the top.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ヒツ | on | [万年筆](../words/万年筆.md) まんねんひつ - fountain pen; [執筆](../words/執筆.md) しっぴつ - writing; authoring; [随筆](../words/随筆.md) ずいひつ - personal essay; [筆記](../words/筆記.md) ひっき - writing down; [筆者](../words/筆者.md) ひっしゃ - writer |\n| ふで | kun | [筆](../words/筆.md) ふで - writing or painting brush |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [筆](../words/筆.md) ふで - writing brush\n- [万年筆](../words/万年筆.md) まんねんひつ - fountain pen\n- [鉛筆](../words/鉛筆.md) えんぴつ - pencil\n- [執筆](../words/執筆.md) しっぴつ - writing; authoring\n- [随筆](../words/随筆.md) ずいひつ - personal essay; literary jottings\n- [筆記](../words/筆記.md) ひっき - writing down; taking notes\n- [筆者](../words/筆者.md) ひっしゃ - writer of a text; author\n\n## Notes\n\n- The linked [筆](../words/筆.md) article teaches ふで. In the linked [万年筆](../words/万年筆.md) article's まんねんひつ reading, 筆 is ヒツ, unlike ぴつ in [鉛筆](../words/鉛筆.md); learn each whole compound. JMdict also records まんねんぴつ and まんねんふで for 万年筆.\n- The dictionary also records ひつ for the spelling 筆. The native noun ふで is still a valid reading; the on example does not replace it.\n- In 執筆, シツ + ヒツ become しっぴつ, with a small っ and ヒ changing to ピ. Learn that whole compound rather than adding ピツ as an independent reading everywhere.\n- In 筆記 and 筆者, ヒツ contracts before キ or シャ to give ひっき and ひっしゃ. Learn these whole compounds; ヒツ does not always contract.\n- Compare [律](律.md), law or rhythm, and [建](建.md), build. [書](書.md), write, is also a useful comparison, but writing meanings overlap, so it is not a safe wrong answer merely because the shape differs.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1178590, 1319710, 1372790, 1487770, 1487800, 1487830, 1526360.\n",
